 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT in relation to granting Tier IV status in the New York state and local\nemployees' retirement system to Vincent Stark",
    "basePrintNo": "S7469",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7469-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7469\n\nSPONSOR: BRESLIN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act in relation to granting Tier IV status in the New York state and\nlocal employees' retirement system to Vincent Stark\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAllows Vincent Stark, who failed to become a member of the New York\nState and Local Employees Retirement System for reasons not ascribable\nto his own negligence, and was employed by the New York State Assembly\nas an intern, to claim a benefit from his original employment start date\nwhen he was an employee of the New York State Assembly.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 allows Vincent Stark to receive a benefit based on the total\nservice credit to which he was entitled at the time of his employment\nstart. Section 2 requires that there shall be no refund of member bene-\nfits to Vincent Stark. Section 3 requires that all costs associated with\nthis act be borne by the state of New York. Section 4 contains the\neffective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nVincent Stark was employed by the New York State Assembly starting from\nJanuary of 2005 to June of 2005. He was eligible the pension system, but\nthrough no fault of his own, did not join at that time. At the time, he\nwould have been eligible for entrance into Tier IV. However, as he was\nnot provided with an application to apply for membership pursuant to\nSection 45 of the Retirement and Social Security Law of 1986, he did not\njoin the system in 2005. Had he entered the pension system in 2005, he\nwould be a member of Tier IV. This bill allows him to retroactively\nenter the pension tier that he was entitled to in 2005.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nFiscal note attached.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately\n",
